From: Michal Frdlik <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] fcstat: read statfs as Linux does on Thylacine

FcFStatFs picks its fstatfs arm from what the configure step found. musl's
struct statfs has f_flags, so the arm is taken; inside it, only a BSD
MNT_LOCAL, an f_fstypename member or __linux__ says how to read the result,
and anything else stops the build with an #error. Thylacine's libc is musl,
whose struct statfs is Linux's, so the Linux reading of f_type (nfs is
remote, fat has a broken mtime) is the one that fits. Pouch's fstatfs
answers ENOSYS today, so FcFStatFs returns -1 and its callers take their
defaults (mmap is safe, mtime is not broken) before the switch is reached.

diff -ruN a/src/fcstat.c b/src/fcstat.c
--- a/src/fcstat.c
+++ b/src/fcstat.c
@@ -372,7 +372,7 @@
 #  endif
 #  if defined(HAVE_STRUCT_STATFS_F_FSTYPENAME)
 	p = buf.f_fstypename;
-#  elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+#  elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) || defined(__thylacine__)
 	switch (buf.f_type) {
 	case 0x6969: /* nfs */
 	    statb->is_remote_fs = FcTrue;
